/** @mainpage Pop3ClientDataProvider Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section pop3clientdataproviderintro Introduction to the Pop3ClientDataProvider Module

    The %Pop3ClientDataProvider module provides a @ref dataproviderintro "data provider" API for POP3 servers.

    This data provider provides Pop3Client API access to:
    - List available messages on the server (with sizes and UIDLs)
    - Retrieve specific messages by ID
    - Retrieve message headers only (more efficient)
    - Get message metadata and content
    - Query server capabilities
    - Get unique message identifiers (UIDL)

    @section pop3clientdataprovider_factory Pop3Client Data Provider Factory

    The name of the Pop3Client data provider factory is <b><tt>pop3</tt></b>.

    @section pop3clientdataprovider_structure Data Provider Structure

    The data provider has the following structure:
    - \c pop3/ - Root data provider
      - \c list - List messages (supports request returning message info with UIDLs)
        - \c {id}/ - Individual message provider
          - \c get - Retrieve full message
          - \c headers - Retrieve headers only (uses TOP command)
      - \c capabilities - Get server capabilities (CAPA command)
      - \c uidl - Get unique message identifiers

    @section pop3clientdataprovider_examples Pop3Client Data Provider Examples

    These examples are with \c qdp, the command-line interface to the Data Provider API, and additionally assume that
    there is an available connection called \c pop3client, which has been fully authorized with OAuth2 to access Pop3Client
    on behalf of the user.

    @par API Example: List Available Messages with UIDLs
    @verbatim qdp pop3client/list
    @endverbatim

    @par API Example: Retrieve a Specific Message
    @verbatim qdp pop3client/list/1/get
    @endverbatim

    @par API Example: Retrieve Only Message Headers
    @verbatim qdp pop3client/list/1/headers
    @endverbatim

    @par API Example: Get Server Capabilities
    @verbatim qdp pop3client/capabilities
    @endverbatim

    @par API Example: Get Unique Message IDs
    @verbatim qdp pop3client/uidl
    @endverbatim

    @section Pop3Clientdataprovider_relnotes Release Notes

    @subsection Pop3Clientdataprovider_v2_1 Pop3ClientDataProvider v2.1
    - Added \c capabilities endpoint for CAPA command (RFC 2449)
    - Added \c uidl endpoint for UIDL command
    - Added \c headers endpoint for efficient header-only retrieval (TOP command)
    - Enhanced \c list endpoint to return message sizes and UIDLs via request

    @subsection Pop3Clientdataprovider_v2_0 Pop3ClientDataProvider v2.0
    - updated for new data provider API

    @subsection Pop3Clientdataprovider_v1_0 Pop3ClientDataProvider v1.0
    - initial release of the module
*/

#! Contains all public definitions in the Pop3ClientDataProvider module
public namespace Pop3ClientDataProvider {
#! Generic Pop3 server app name
public const AppName = "Pop3";

public const Pop3LogoWhite = File::readTextFile(get_script_dir() + "/pop3-logo-white.svg");
}
